            "text": "{\"strengths\":[\"Clear causal chain: drought reduces harvests, shifting supply left while demand remains unchanged.\",\"Accurately explains the shortage at the original equilibrium price and the adjustment to a higher price.\",\"Correctly concludes that equilibrium price rises and equilibrium quantity traded falls.\"],\"improvements\":[\"Include the required demand-and-supply diagram, with unchanged D, supply shifting left from S1 to S2, and both equilibria labelled P1/P2 and Q1/Q2.\"],\"mistakes\":[\"Missing required diagram\"],\"examinerComment\":\"Your written explanation is economically accurate and complete: reduced wheat availability shifts supply left, causing a shortage at the old price, a rise in price, and a fall in equilibrium quantity. However, this question explicitly requires a diagram, and no image was submitted, so diagram marks cannot be awarded. Prioritise adding a clearly labelled wheat-market diagram.\",\"studyNext\":\"Practise drawing a supply-decrease diagram: label the axes Price of wheat and Quantity of wheat, keep D unchanged, shift S1 left to S2, and mark the two equilibrium prices and quantities.\",\"assessmentFormat\":\"paper_2_c_to_f_diagram_and_explanation\",\"paper\":\"paper_2\",\"questionPart\":\"c\",\"levelRelevance\":\"shared_sl_hl\",\"assessmentSkills\":[\"diagram_explanation\",\"economic_analysis\",\"application\"],\"commandTerm\":\"explain\",\"commandTermLabel\":\"Using a demand and supply diagram, explain\",\"syllabusUnit\":\"unit_2\",\"syllabusTopic\":\"2.3\",\"topicLabel\":\"Competitive market equilibrium\",\"classificationConfidence\":\"high\",\"markingConfidence\":\"high\",\"diagramExpected\":true,\"diagramSubmitted\":false,\"diagramAssessmentStatus\":\"not_submitted\",\"workingsExpected\":false,\"workingsSubmitted\":false,\"workingsAssessmentStatus\":\"not_relevant\",\"attachmentContent\":\"none\",\"assessableEarned\":2,\"markBreakdown\":[{\"label\":\"Economic analysis\",\"awarded\":4,\"available\":4,\"reason\":\"The prose gives a complete and accurate adjustment process from reduced harvests to lower supply, shortage, higher price and lower equilibrium quantity.\"},{\"label\":\"Application to context\",\"awarded\":4,\"available\":4,\"reason\":\"The explanation applies directly to wheat, the drought, unchanged demand and the initial equilibrium stated in the scenario.\"},{\"label\":\"Diagram\",\"awarded\":0,\"available\":4,\"reason\":\"No diagram was submitted, so the required supply shift and labelled equilibria cannot be assessed.\"}],\"bandRationale\":null,\"limitations\":[],\"componentEvaluation\":{\"diagram\":0,\"explanation\":2,\"diagramReason\":\"No diagram was submitted; therefore there is no visual evidence of the required unchanged demand curve, leftward supply shift, or equilibrium outcomes.\",\"explanationReason\":\"Accurately explains that drought reduces supply at each price, creates a shortage at the old price, raises equilibrium price and lowers quantity traded.\",\"incompatibleMechanisms\":false,\"mismatchEvidence\":\"\",\"labelingDeficiency\":false,\"labelingEvidence\":\"\",\"rootErrors\":[]}}"
          }
